# The monogamy of entanglement, read through the CHSH game. A pair sharing a maximally entangled state can violate the
# Bell-CHSH inequality up to the Tsirelson bound, two root two, whose square is eight, past the classical limit of two
# whose square is four. But this strength cannot be shared: the Toner-Verstraete relation bounds the two CHSH values one
# party can hold with two partners, the sum of their squares at most eight, so a maximal bridge to one partner forces the
# other to zero. The two partners a central party is entangled with play symmetric roles in this bound. This file MODELS
# the two partners and DEFINES the swap that exchanges them, then PROVES the swap is an involution, so the monogamy bound
# is symmetric in the two partners. The Tsirelson square, the quantum-beats-classical gap, and both faces of the monogamy
# sum reaching eight are recorded as machine-integer facts. The symmetry is proved over the actual partner type by
# induction.

# The two partners a central party can be entangled with.
form partner
  case first
  case second

# The swap exchanging the two partners, under which the monogamy bound is symmetric.
task swap
  take p, like partner
  like partner
  fork case, read p
    case first
      send back
        make second
    case second
      send back
        make first

# THE SWAP IS AN INVOLUTION: exchanging the two partners twice returns them, swap (swap p) = p, for every partner, so the
# monogamy bound, the sum of the two squared CHSH values, does not depend on which partner is named first. Proved by
# induction over the two partners.
rule the-partner-swap-is-an-involution
  seat p, like partner
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call swap
        call swap
          read p
      read p
  fold p

# THE TSIRELSON BOUND SQUARED is eight, the quantum ceiling on a single CHSH value: (2 root 2) squared is 4 * 2 = 8, as a
# machine-integer fact.
hold tsirelson-bound-squared-is-eight
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      code 4
      code 2

# QUANTUM BEATS CLASSICAL: the classical CHSH bound squared is four, below the quantum eight, 4 below 8.
hold quantum-beats-classical
  call is-below
    code 4
    code 8

# MONOGAMY AT THE SINGLET CORNER: the first pair takes the full squared strength eight, forcing the second to zero,
# 8 + 0 = 8, a maximal bridge to one partner and none to a third.
hold a-maximal-bridge-forbids-a-third
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call add
      code 8
      code 0

# CLASSICAL CORRELATION SHARES BOTH WAYS: two classical values of squared strength four each fill the same budget,
# 4 + 4 = 8, so classical correlation can be held with both partners at once while a quantum throat cannot.
hold classical-correlation-shares-both-ways
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call add
      code 4
      code 4
